WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the 62-second MFAS resident film.
Timings are the narration's own measured per-line start and end times, taken from the
film build (vo/timings.json), not estimated by ear. The narration is machine-generated
speech (Google Gemini TTS, voice "Charon"): it is not a recording of a person, and no
part of it is anyone's spoken testimony.

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.425
If your property tax went up this year, you
probably wanted to know why.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.745
The answer sits in two budgets,

3
00:00:08.745 --> 00:00:13.970
from two governments — six documents, a
thousand pages.

4
00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:18.250
So somebody read them, and put the answers
in one place.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.749
Type in your home's value, and it shows what
you actually pay.

6
00:00:24.749 --> 00:00:27.430
The town's share, and the county's.

7
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.795
The county's share is larger because it buys
schools, the sheriff and ambulances.

8
00:00:35.045 --> 00:00:36.752
Enter your own water use,

9
00:00:36.752 --> 00:00:40.780
and the bill is calculated from the town's
published rates.

10
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:45.930
It shows what the town funded this year, and
what it turned down.

11
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:54.950
Every figure names the document and the page
it came from. So you can check it.

12
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.540
Your town. Your money. Take a look.
